        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-12 20:07:49.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: start and stop conf-sanity MDTs in parallel",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: start and stop conf-sanity MDTs in parallel\n\nconf-sanity starts and stops its MDTs through its own start_mds() and\nstop_mds(), one after another, so the parallel mount and unmount in\nsetupall() and stopall() do not reach them.  The suite starts and\nstops the MDTs around 250 times per run, and with four MDTs each\nstart costs about 6 seconds.\n\nStart them with start_facets() and stop them with unmount_facets(),\nwhich come from the parent patches \"LU-17240 tests: unmount targets\nin parallel\" and \"LU-17240 tests: start targets through shared\nstart_facets()\".  MDT0000 still starts first, and start_mds() still\nreturns 94 at once if it fails.  stop_mds() now stops every MDT\nbefore it returns 97 for a failure.  cleanup_nocli() still stops\nOST0000 before the MDTs.  PARALLEL_MOUNT=0 and PARALLEL_UMOUNT=0\nkeep the serial order.\n\nunmount_facets() also removes $TMP/<facet>active, so in a failover\nconfiguration an MDT that a subtest failed over (27b, 47a) is next\nstarted on its primary node, as after stopall().  It also tries to\nunload dm-flakey on the servers, which fails harmlessly while a\ndm-flakey device is still in use.\n\nOn a VM cluster with 4 MDTs on 2 MDS nodes, conf-sanity 0 1 2 3 5a\n17 24a 27b 41a 41c 47a 50a 84 124 took 967 s before and 722 s\nafter (-25%), with the same results (13 pass, 2 skip); the run\nmade 81 parallel MDT starts and 172 parallel MDT stops.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity\nTest-Parameters: mdtcount=4 mdscount=2 testlist=conf-sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I708d6d1aa0f3df36f176f84f0f364b38b078e353\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
